trong>SCP-5161-B</strong> is a full-grown Cauliflower (Brassica oleracea var. botrytis) and appears to have the same qualities as SCP-5161-A. SCP-5161 instances are to be kept in the same containment cell, instances seem to hold each other in high regard.</p> <p>SCP-5161-B has been retrieved in 1994 in █████, Norway. Foundation agent ████ █████ has retrieved instance from a local supermarket. No breach of secrecy has occured and object has been safely retrieved at Site-██. Instances seem to have acknowledge some sort of family bond even though testing has shown instances do not seem to understand each other verbally. Anomalous means of communicating are expected.</p> <p>SCP-5161-B appears to be sapient and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 6 (six). Drawings and letters are present, though these are written in Norwegian. SCP-5161 instances seem to have a language barrier between each other, ongoing studies have to show how these instances communicate with this barrier. Ongoing anomalous means are currently suspected.</p> <p><strong>SCP-5161-C</strong> is a full-grown parsnip (Pastinaca sativa) and has been in foundation custody since 201█. Subject has been retrieved from Site-██’s cafeteria. An unknown foundation personnel has brought subject into Site-██. During lunchbreak SCP-5161-C got severely distressed resulting in SCP-5161-C event (see addendum SCP-5161-C)</p> <p>Unknown foundation personnel brought SCP-5161-C from home to consume during lunchbreak. Current studies have shown to trigger severe distress from subject when in view of a sharp object, such as a knife. It is currently not known how SCP-5161-C sees the world around it, since no senses have been shown during testing.</p> <p>Origins of SCP-5161-C are not known, because the foundation personnel that brought it into the facility has died during SCP-5161-C event and the containment breach that occurred during this episode. Subject appears to be sapient and exhibits intelligence and common knowledge consistent with that of a human child aged 2 (two). Testing has shown no unusual qualities to make it discernible from a non-sapient parsnip.</p> <p>Drawings are produced by SCP-5161-C but lack severely in quality as expected of a small child. Current drawings offer no conclusion to the origin of subject, language or other significant details.</p> <p>During the last years all three instances of SCP-5161 seem to have bonded together. It is currently unknown if all instances spark from the same origin, though this does seem to be unlikely since subjects were found in different countries and different years.</p> <p>By unknown anomalous means (suspected telepathy) are instances ‘able to communicate’ with each other. It is unknown what instances tell each other, if they even speak. It is not known how these instances communicate since they do not appear to speak each other languages.</p> <p><strong>Addendum SCP-5161-C</strong><br /> An unknown foundation personnel brought SCP-5161-C into containment, unknowingly, on 16-9-201█. During lunchbreak subject was experiencing increasing levels of trauma causing distress. Current theory is the subject startled in view of the knife, testing afterwards seems to cause the same effect but less dramatic when close to other SCP-5161 instances.</p> <p>Current SCP-5161 instances were known to have access to anomalous means, most notably telekinesis. The same effect is present in SCP-5161-C but far stronger especially observed during this event. Priorly unknown to the foundation the subject also able to put out a regional electromagnetic pulse blast (EMP) resulting in the containment breach of six (6) other SCP’s. This effect cost the lives of ██ foundation personnel while injuring ██ more.</p> <p>Camera’s and surveillance footage were unable to be reviewed as any live cameras were destroyed in the process of the episode. Due to unavailable footage it is currently not known who brought SCP-5161-C into Site-██. Investigations to retain other footage through interviews is still ongoing.</p> <p>Nearby MTF units were able to re-contain the other assets within approximately three (3) hours. During these hours another ██ foundation personnel were lost; making in total ██ lost foundation personnel while another ██ were injured during the process.</p> <p>Because of this event SCP-5161 instances have to be kept in a docile state and content in their containment cell. Object class has been promoted to Euclid by the approval of Dr. █████ and 05-█.</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raptorverhoeven" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7130596&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608173785" alt="RaptorVerhoeven" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7130596)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raptorverhoeven" >RaptorVerhoeven</a></span></p> 
