						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>Item number: SCP-5181</p> <p>Object class: Euclid</p> <p>Special containment procedures: SCP-5181 must be kept in a 30 by 30&#160;cm box lined with strong synthetic padding.<br /> The sealed box is then submerged in the center of the 10&#160;m by 10&#160;m polyethylene holding tank.<br /> it should be sufficient to decrease the kinetic activity of SCP-5181 for adequate recovery by containment personnel.<br /> All personnel entering the SCP-5181 containment chamber must wear specialized coating (found in Note SCP-5181)<br /> and one and a breathing apparatus before being lowered into the polyethylene tank. and a breathing apparatus before being lowered into the polyethylene tank.<br /> If SCP-5181 is loose outside the polyethylene tank, personnel are advised to protect themselves in a separate room and close the doors.<br /> or hatches to isolate SCP-5181 until the arrival of the containment teams.<br /> [quarter past eleven]<br /> Description: SCP-5181 has the appearance of a &quot;Beyblade&quot; manufactured by the company OLM in 1997. It is six (6) centimeters in diameter and is red.<br /> At first considered a pleasant and harmless child's toy, SCP-5181 was able to spin up to 3,000 times its normal speed, making it an authentic<br /> metal tornado capable of reaching about 3,000 times its normal speed. CP-5181 was found by founding agents in the city of ███████ em ███████<br /> after several reports from the population of a metal &quot;mini tornado&quot; it destroyed several houses and caused more than three deaths and several injured. According to reports by<br /> SCP-5181 Foundation<br /> it simply stopped spinning after 3 days when it fell into a lake near the city of ███████. Tests made with SCP-5181 reveal that it is made of a metal of unknown origin,<br /> but almost twice the strength of steel and will not rust.</p> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vito-loureiro" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6992467&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608173787" alt="Vito loureiro" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6992467)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/vito-loureiro" >Vito loureiro</a></span></p> 
